if you're like me then you like to take  your switch with you and play it  everywhere on your tv  airplanes while you're laying in bed at  2am and should be sleeping or while  you're pooping  i mean if you really want to keep  watching you can  so that means when i have the option and  a game is multi-platform i tend to favor  picking it up on my switch  you know because of the whole pooping  thing but as we all know this machine is  a little behind the xbox series x slash  s and ps5  and playstation 4 and xbox one so with  gta trilogy the definitive edition just  having released the question is should  you pick it up on the switch i mean  they're old games from the ps2 era what  could possibly go wrong  oh my god  oh no  oh no  to quickly save you some time if you  plan to play the game portably then sure  why not it's a serviceable enough  version  but if you plan to primarily play the  game docked and on your tv then  no  definitely go with another version  i'm saying that up front so hey for  those of you who don't want to blow the  video to give you a quick answer i'm  saving you some time but if you'd like  to know why here's the deal while these  are ps2 remakes the graphics were  enhanced even if some of the results  were  uh  let's say unintentionally hilarious at  times  but the graphics are far better on the  non-switch versions and honestly while i  know it's not as powerful of a system i  don't totally understand why as the  graphics for the gta trilogy don't  exactly seem all that great  i mean take crash bandicoot insane  trilogy the graphics for that look far  more impressive than gta although  granted a giant open world isn't being  loaded at once but still the game looks  similar enough on the switch  but if you compare the gta trilogy  everything looks much better outside of  the switch especially the environments  when i was playing vice city on my ps5  with those sweet pink and blue retro 80s  tones coming in from the sky vice city  actually looked pretty gorgeous that was  when the game truly shone and it felt  like an actual enhancement from the  original games meanwhile on my switch  it just doesn't look as impressive  on top of that despite having worse  graphics the loading times were also  slightly worse on the switch  there's a ghosting issue on both  versions where you can see ghosting  behind your car and it's especially  noticeable behind a motorcycle and this  issue seemed to be more pronounced on  the switch  additionally the draw distance on  objects like cars you might run into or  ramps you might shoot off of is  unreasonably bad the switch also doesn't  have as many graphic modes that you can  adjust compared to other versions on my  ps5 i could turn on and off lens flare  motion blur and depth of field whereas  none of these settings are available on  the switch additionally you can toggle  between performance and fidelity  graphics modes so if the game is getting  a little laggy on fidelity mode just  flip on performance mode and you should  be good to go  but if you're like me and don't care too  much about graphics there is another  far more major issue i ran into  and that was a consistent frame drop and  lag while driving around the city in any  of the gta games it didn't matter if i  was driving around liberty city  vice city  [Music]  you could be certain that i would  consistently be battling against lag no  matter how much i tried to adjust the  graphical setting to try and make the  game run better and for a game series  called grand theft auto where the  primary thing you're doing uh in between  murdering people with chainsaws getting  hookers and blowing up buildings is  driving that's really what the core of  the game has been and this frame drop  issue was brutal when you're chasing  down and trying to run over a pizza man  within a strict time limit who somehow  delivers his pizzas by randomly throwing  them at the ground the last thing you  want to worry about is the lag and frame  drops causing you to crash into another  set of cars it was honestly that bad and  that frustrating and this lag i'm  showing you wasn't even the worst case  i'm going to show you my footage  unedited from vice city's mission  demolition man where i had to blow up a  building  with  what  meanwhile this is how it looks on a ps5  so given all of this  why am i giving the game a pass on the  switch  that was good timing specifically it's  because oddly enough the game actually  runs better in handheld mode i first  played the game docked so i could record  footage and wrongly assumed that would  be the best way to play the game  but once i later hopped in bed to play  the game suddenly the lag and frame  drops while driving were gone i did go  ahead and replay the game all the way  through the demolition man stage just to  test out blowing up the building again  as that was the worst case of frame  drops and  it still had frame drops during the  explosion  but up until then the game had performed  reasonably well i was actually pretty  satisfied with it and when i later  booted up gta san andreas oh [ __ ] here  we go again i didn't have any noticeable  issues  at least in the limited time i played it  to be perfectly transparent i didn't get  early access so i purchased the game on  the switch and got a review code for the  ps5 day of and i tried to play a decent  chunk of all three games on both systems  so i could do my best to accurately  compare them so in the end if you're  dying to play the gta trilogy on your  switch handheld  it's okay and while the frame drops in  dock mode are super annoying and  definitely not something i'm giving a  pass the game is still playable while  docked so if the nintendo switch is your  only option  hey you can still play it on the switch  but if you do want to play the game on a  tv primarily  yeah i'd say skip the switch version and  enjoy laughing at the ridiculous  character models that also exist in the  ps5 version of the game i hope this  helped and i'll see you guys next time  peace  [Music]  do  [Music]  you
 

